---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import ReviewNote from '../../../components/ReviewNote.astro';
import CharityNetworkDirectory from '../../../components/CharityNetworkDirectory.astro';
import { networkGuides, entriesForGuide } from '../../../data/charity-network-guides.mjs';
import { url } from '../../../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Charity networks, founder programs and leadership communities" description="Find charity founder programs, leadership communities and umbrella networks. Sourced guides explain who each serves, how to engage and what to check.">
  <header class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><Crumbs items={[{label:'For charities',href:'/for-charities/'},{label:'Networks'}]} /><p class="eyebrow">The infrastructure around generosity · editorial draft</p><h1>Good work needs<br />good connections.</h1><p class="lede">Find peers, founder support and organizations that connect the sector. Start with the kind of help you need, then check the fit.</p><div class="network-actions"><a class="btn" href="#directory">Explore the directory</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href={url('/for-charities/collaborate/')}>Help shape Charitology</a></div></div></header>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="intro prose section-tight"><h2>What do these groups do?</h2><p>Some support a founder. Others connect chief executives, represent a sector, maintain local directories or provide professional learning. “Meta-charity” is useful shorthand here for work supporting the system around charities; it is not a legal status or a claim these organizations share one philosophy.</p><p>This selected directory summarizes official sources. Each entry explains its audience, geography, access and limits. Inclusion and numbering are not ratings, endorsements or evidence of a relationship with Charitology. Program selection, fees and membership conditions belong to the organization and may change.</p></section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="guides-title"><p class="eyebrow">Read an annotated guide</p><h2 id="guides-title">Three ways into the field.</h2><div class="guide-grid">{networkGuides.map(g => <a class="guide-card" href={url(`/for-charities/networks/${g.id}/`)}><span class="guide-count">{entriesForGuide(g).length} starting points</span><h3>{g.title}</h3><p>{g.description}</p><span>Read the guide →</span></a>)}</div></section>
    <div id="directory" class="section-tight"><CharityNetworkDirectory /></div>
    <section class="section-tight prose network-next"><h2>Bring a question, then keep what you learn.</h2><p>Ask how others handle a specific job: welcoming a donor, assigning a task, finding a local partner or testing an assumption. Participation should respect the group’s purpose and rules. A membership or contact link is not an invitation for unsolicited promotion.</p><p>Use the <a href={url('/for-charities/fundraising/')}>fundraising hub</a> for methods and follow-up planning. In <a href="https://os.charitology.org/#module/resources">Charity OS Resources</a>, you can manually record a useful reference; <a href="https://os.charitology.org/#module/projects">Projects and tasks</a> can give the next step an owner. These links open modules after sign-in and organization choice. They do not copy this directory, join a network or contact anyone.</p><p>Know a missing or changed listing? <a href="https://github.com/theguysaccount/charitology/issues/new?template=charity-network.yml">Suggest a network or correction</a> with an official source. GitHub issues are public; use organization-level links and leave private contact details out.</p></section>
    <ReviewNote filePath="src/data/charity-networks.mjs" title="Charity networks directory" />
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  h1{max-width:16ch}.intro{max-width:75ch}.network-actions{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1.5rem}.guide-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.guide-card{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:var(--radius);background:var(--surface);text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}.guide-card:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}.guide-card h3{font-size:1.6rem;margin:.7rem 0}.guide-card p{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:1rem}.guide-count,.guide-card>span:last-child{font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--accent)}.guide-card>span:last-child{margin-top:auto}.network-next{border-top:1px solid var(--rule);max-width:75ch}#directory{scroll-margin-top:5rem}a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:800px){.guide-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
